//! Total finite classical functions, implemented as ordinary checked source.
//!
//! These functions take ordinary labels, including already measured Bit results.
//! They cannot inspect live quantum owners or perform observation.
//! Runtime argument effects remain in the caller. Importing or calling these
//! helpers grants no quantum primitive, access or verification privilege.
//! Contracts and finite regression status: Contract identifiers: B001-B002.

/// Return x xor y for all four pairs of Bit inputs.
/// This two-argument map is total but not injective on the product domain.
/// A coherent lift must check injectivity of its complete enclosing map.
pub classical fn xor2(x: Bit, y: Bit) -> Bit { x xor y }

/// Return x and y for all four pairs of Bit inputs.
/// This total, noninjective predicate can describe reversible XOR computation
/// into an auxiliary; calling it does not measure a quantum register.
pub classical fn and2(x: Bit, y: Bit) -> Bit { x and y }
